{"id":"dough","name":"Dough","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:dough"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Dough","text":"(batsek, meaning “swelling,” i.e., in fermentation). The dough the Israelites had prepared for baking was carried away by them out of Egypt in their kneading-troughs (Ex. 12:34, 39). In the process of baking, the dough had to be turned (Hos. 7:8)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6182","lemma":"עֲרִיסָה","xlit":"ʻărîyçâh","gloss":"meal","kjv":"dough","count":4,"share":0.57},{"strong":"H8641","lemma":"תְּרוּמָה","xlit":"tᵉrûwmâh","gloss":"a present , especially in sacrifice or as tribute","kjv":"gift, heave offering, oblation, offered","count":5,"share":0.71},{"strong":"H7225","lemma":"רֵאשִׁית","xlit":"rêʼshîyth","gloss":"the first, in place, time, order or rank","kjv":"beginning, chief, first, principal thing","count":4,"share":0.57},{"strong":"H3888","lemma":"לוּשׁ","xlit":"lûwsh","gloss":"to knead","kjv":"knead","count":2,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H1217","lemma":"בָּצֵק","xlit":"bâtsêq","gloss":"dough","kjv":"dough, flour","count":2,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H1197","lemma":"בָּעַר","xlit":"bâʻar","gloss":"to kindle","kjv":"be brutish, bring  away, burn, eat","count":2,"share":0.29}],"verses":["Num.15.20","Num.15.21","Neh.10.37","Ezek.44.30","Num.15.19","Jer.7.18","Hos.7.4"],"related":[{"id":"bread","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"oven","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"heave-offering","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.07,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"first-fruits","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.055,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"bread","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.028,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"heave-offering","type":"lexical","strong":"H8641","why":"both lead with תְּרוּמָה (H8641)"}],"works":[{"work":"philo","title":"The Works of Philo Judaeus",